{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"eb47294117ce2001","name":"card_event_maginot_line","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/France/events/card_event_maginot_line","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"MAGINOT LINE","text":"Give target ground unit +3+4 and \"Cannot retreat or be suppressed.\"","flavorText":"Built between the two World Wars, the Maginot Line was one of the most ambitious defensive systems ever constructed. Stretching over 400 kilometers from Switzerland to Luxembourg, it was designed to shield France from a future German invasion. Named after French Minister of War André Maginot, the line featured a network of underground fortresses, bunkers, artillery casemates, and supply tunnels. Each major fortification, or “ouvrage”, could house hundreds of soldiers and came equipped with retractable turrets, machine guns, and anti-tank weapons. Deep underground, these forts contained living quarters, power plants, command centers, and even electric railways to transport ammunition. The goal was to delay or block any direct assault on France’s eastern border, buying time for full mobilization.\r\nThe Maginot Line reflected the trauma of World War I and France’s desperate desire to avoid another devastating invasion. It stood as a symbol of national resilience and engineering prowess, intended to turn the eastern frontier into an impenetrable wall. While the defense strategy would later be bypassed, the construction itself remains a remarkable feat of military planning.","faction":"France","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":3,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_maginot_line","title":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_maginot_line_title","SourceString":"MAGINOT LINE","LocalizedString":"MAGINOT LINE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::France","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_maginot_line_text","SourceString":"Give target gro