ons. Deep underground, these forts contained living quarters, power plants, command centers, and even electric railways to transport ammunition. The goal was to delay or block any direct assault on France’s eastern border, buying time for full mobilization.\r\nThe Maginot Line reflected the trauma of World War I and France’s desperate desire to avoid another devastating invasion. It stood as a symbol of national resilience and engineering prowess, intended to turn the eastern frontier into an impenetrable wall. While the defense strategy would later be bypassed, the construction itself remains a remarkable feat of military planning."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","isInPermanentPool":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_2.0"},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/MAGINOT_LINE.MAGINOT_LINE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":381.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_maginot_line_photo","SourceString":"French troops being transported by rail through a tunnel in the Maginot Line. Ca. 1939.","LocalizedString":"French troops being transported by rail through a tunnel in the Maginot Line. Ca. 1939."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"Notes":"Image needed to be customized","isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_maginot_line_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pure":false,"event":